      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine its length and width. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\nGiven the information:\n1. Walking the length 25 times would cover 1000 meters.\n2. Walking the perimeter 10 times would also cover 1000 meters.\n\nFrom the first piece of information:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( L \\):\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nFrom the second piece of information, the perimeter of the backyard is:\n\\[ 2L + 2W = 1000 \\]\nSince we already know \\( L = 40 \\), we can substitute this value into the equation:\n\\[ 2(40) + 2W = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 80 + 2W = 1000 \\]\nSubtract 80 from both sides:\n\\[ 2W = 920 \\]\nSolving for \\( W \\):\n\\[ W = \\frac{920}{2} = 460 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNow that we have both the length and the width, we can find the area of the backyard. The area \\( A \\) is given by:\n\\[ A = L \\times W = 40 \\times 460 = 18400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{18400}\\).",
