      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard, we need to determine its dimensions. We are given two pieces of information about the backyard:\n\n1. Walking the length 25 times results in a distance of 1000 meters.\n2. Walking the perimeter 10 times also results in a distance of 1000 meters.\n\nLet's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\n### Step 1: Write the equations based on the given information\n\nFrom the first piece of information:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\n\nFrom the second piece of information:\n\\[ 10 \\times (2L + 2W) = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 2L + 2W = 100 \\]\n\\[ L + W = 50 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Solve for \\( L \\) and \\( W \\)\n\nFirst, solve the equation \\( 25L = 1000 \\) for \\( L \\):\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} \\]\n\\[ L = 40 \\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( L = 40 \\) into the equation \\( L + W = 50 \\):\n\\[ 40 + W = 50 \\]\n\\[ W = 10 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the area of the backyard\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[ A = L \\times W \\]\n\nSubstitute the values of \\( L \\) and \\( W \\):\n\\[ A = 40 \\times 10 \\]\n\\[ A = 400 \\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
